  "Question": "When \\(x=2\\), find the value of \\(\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot x\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "First calculate inside the parentheses: \\(1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\\). Then multiply by \\(2\\) to get \\(3\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the distributive law\n\nDistributing the factor \\(x\\) makes the reciprocal product equal to \\(1\\). Since \\(x=2\\ne0\\),\n\\[\n\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)x=x+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot x=x+1.\n\\]\nAt \\(x=2\\), the value is \\(2+1=3\\).",
